  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asia Pacific Leaders Malaria Alliance Core Contributions 2018-19 to 2027-28</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment provides core contributions to the Secretariat of the Asia Pacific Leaders Malaria Alliance (APLMA) and Asia Pacific Malaria Elimination Network (APMEN) Secretariat. APLMA-APMEN support a range of activities to advance the goal of eliminating malaria across the Asia-Pacific region by 2030, based on strategic themes identified in APLMA&apos;s 10 year strategy: leadership for impact, financing for sustainability, strengthening health systems against public health threats, data for decision-making, partnerships for synergies, and access for equity. Based in Singapore, the joint APLMA-APMEN Secretariat works across the region, with a focus on priority countries in the Greater Mekong Subregion (Cambodia, Thailand, Vietnam), Melanesia (PNG, Solomon Islands, Vanuatu), Timor-Leste, Indonesia and India. In 2023 this investment was extended following a design refresh to incorporate a new agreement with APLMA from 2022-23 to 2026-27 (#77928).</narrative>
  </description>
